  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati Disability Support Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kiribati Disability Support Program aligns with Australia&apos;s International Development Policy in ensuring we remain a strong and consistent advocate for disability equity and rights. 
The 2015 Kiribati Census confirmed that 14% of the total population in Kiribati has some form of disability. The Kiribati School and Centre for Children with Disabilities (KSCCD) is the only existing institution that provides education for children with a disability. 
This investment will focus on the delivery of multi-year program of support to the Kiribati School and Centre for Children with Disabilities. The objective of the investment is to ensure: i) ongoing operation and delivery of quality inclusive education; ii) children&#x2019;s access to the school on a daily basis; and iii) ongoing support for mainstreaming initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
